    # callable formal calls whichever method the actual names, and that method may throw its implicit names (and the
    # contract's declared ones, which every method reaching the formal shares, S1.4).  The contract -- a descriptor-only
    # method, with no body for l2_body_throws to read -- is on the status channel (a conservative ABI, an
    # implementation choice, as for a held call), marked here, after l2_body_throws computed the marks and before
    # l2_throws_close closes the callers over it through the call edge above, as over any callee; the site then reads
    # the selected callee's ordinal (l2_emit_dyn_tail) and routes it as a call's (l2_emit_propagate with the
    # contract's d).  Before: the site's "a callable that cannot throw reported a status" invariant aborted on the
    # callee's ordinary throw.
    if: check_unevaluated_cell[0] = 0 && fi >= 0 && m_throws_cell[0] != 0
        m_throws_cell[0][idx]: 1
    # THE ENTRY RECEPTION (lmx_walk.h, LMX_WALK_SOURCE_RECEPTION): the callee a call selects receives its Structure
    # formals itself, at its entry, by its own records, and a refusal there is the call's `implements`.  A call through
    # a value (a model's callable field: a bodyless method's description) selects a callee this translation does not
    # see, so nothing here proved that reception: this method reads the call's status, as at an admission site.  A
    # call through a callable formal is on the status channel already (above).
